ART. 102. Liability for Service Quality Imperfection. - The service supplier is liable for any quality imperfections that render the services improper for consumption or decrease their value, and for those resulting from inconsistency with the information contained in the offer or advertisement, the consumer being entitled to demand alternative at his option:
the performance of the services, without any additional cost and when applicable;

the immediate reimbursement of the amount paid, with monetary updating without prejudice to losses and damages, if any;

a proportionate price reduction.
Reperformance of services may be entrusted to duly qualified third parties, at the supplier's risk and cost.

Improper services are those which prove to be inadequate for purposes reasonably expected of them and those that fail to meet the provisions of this Act regulating service rendering.

